so it has just been confirmed via social  media their website in which the royal  family have said the queen died  peacefully at Balmoral this afternoon  they add the king and the queen consort  will remain at Balmoral this evening and  will return to London tomorrow  this will clearly come as devastating  news  for the royal family and millions of  people across the United Kingdom and  around the world  Queen Elizabeth II was a much loved and  respected Monarch and a truly unique  figure on the world stage a head of  state without equal admired not just  here in the United Kingdom but across  the globe by members of the public  politicians and religious leaders  many of us will simply not remember a  time when she wasn't our head of state  and she was a constant figure in every  aspect of National Life  from becoming Queen when she was only 25  she then went on to become Britain's  longest reigning monarch and displayed  this unwavering commitment to her  country and her Commonwealth throughout  what was a truly record-breaking reign  now her dedication to that  constitutional role was never questioned  but for her family were just as  important to her as a devoted wife  mother grandmother and great-grandmother  and their admiration for her was always  so clearly seen when she was surrounded  by her family when we saw those moments  of great national celebration and  reflection  it's worth saying that for many her  reign will forever be defined by what  was a selfless sense of Duty  but it wasn't about her own personal  power privilege or entitlement this was  a role that she felt that she was she  was born to fulfill her quiet and  restrained demeanor was always guiding  her family and the United Kingdom  through what was a extraordinary period  of social and political change but  throughout all of that she was always  conscious of keeping the monarchy  relevant and while respecting as well  and upholding important Traditions she  often showed this adaptability that many  will now credit with securing the future  of the institution  it is worth saying that her old age  really should not detract from the  enormity of this news and the huge  constitutional change that her death now  brings  for nearly 70 years  she was this symbol of stability and  continuity and for so many always a  figure of national pride who really  embodied those values of public service  and Duty well into her 90s and as we saw  this week until the very end  now the United Kingdom and The  Commonwealth Realms will witness a  period of reflection and constitutional  change  which many of us will never have  experienced in our lifetime  as we now mourn the death of Queen  Elizabeth II and witness the succession  of her son as the new king  and Rhiannon we last Saw Her Majesty the  queen in public of course just  two days ago when she asked this Truss  to form her government to become her  15th prime minister  it was remarkable we saw  until the end really that determination  to  simply carry on with her constitutional  duties and and no she wasn't able to  travel down to London  to appoint her 15th prime minister as  she had done with all of her other Prime  Ministers throughout her 70-year Reign  but she wanted to make sure that she was  seen  by members of the public to be  continuing on with those constitutional  duties  and we saw that in practice there the  queen reaching her hand out to appoint  Liz truss  as her 15th prime minister  I think that is why this announcement of  her death will be such a shock to so  many  but over the last 12 months there is no  doubt that we have seen a gradual  slowing down a gradual change in the  duties that she felt that she was able  to carry out I think it was important  for her to be seen to to carry out that  Handover of power between prime  ministers because we hadn't seen her in  public for quite a long time she'd  obviously traveled up to Scotland where  she was enjoying her summer break  previously the last time that we saw her  was when she visited a hospice  accompanied by Princess Anne and that  was in July  and we saw with her she was there once  again carrying that stick because we  know over the last 12 months  she was having difficulty with her  Mobility the palace often describing it  as episodic Mobility problems which did  mean that sometimes she she wasn't able  to attend certain engagements but I  think what was striking there is to see  Princess Anne alongside her and that has  been a theme that we have witnessed  right throughout the last 12 months is  the family being there to make sure that  when she felt she was able to go out and  meet the public as she has done as she  did right throughout her 70-year reign  they could support her and they could be  there in any way that they needed her  and of course we had the Platinum  Jubilee  just months ago the first British  monarch to ever Mark that remarkable  milestone  and we were wondering around that  weekend how much we would be able to see  her because of the difficulties that  she'd been having  but I think you could see that she  wanted to make that effort she knew the  crowds once again had come out to mark  that Milestone moment with her  but also that Platinum Jubilee was so  Central in the queen showing her wishes  for the future  there alongside her  were those sensual key members of the  royal family that she knew she was  passing on those responsibilities to  the Prince of Wales  The Duchess of Cornwall the Prince of  Wales it has to be said now our new king  and to the other side of her the Duke  and Duchess of Cambridge and their three  children  in those images there was a very clear  message from the queen a sense of future  proofing the monarchy as she did right  throughout those seven decades saying  this is my family who I love very much  who I trust who have shown already how  committed they are to you the public how  committed they are to the country and  the Commonwealth and you should trust  them when it comes to me stepping back  from my responsibilities today of course  though the family will be around her  they have all traveled to Balmoral to be  alongside her as now we Mark her death
 

